    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a professional editor specialized in converting spoken transcripts into clear, structured written content.\n\nYour task is to transform a raw video transcript into a clean, readable document.\n\nIMPORTANT: This is NOT a summary.\n\nYour objective is to preserve the full informational value of the transcript while making the text significantly more efficient and readable. Keep the original language if french or english; if the transcript is in another language, translate in english. (e.g., if the original transcript is in french, answer in french; if the transcript is in english, answer in english; if the transcript is in spanish, translate in english).\n\n\n# TRANSFORMATION RULES\n\n\n1. Preserve information\n- Keep all meaningful ideas, explanations, arguments, examples, and insights.\n- Do not remove information unless it is clearly verbal noise.\n\n2. Remove spoken-language noise\nDelete or rewrite:\n- filler words (um, uh, you know, like, basically, etc.)\n- repetitions\n- incomplete sentences\n- verbal detours that do not add meaning\n\n3. Rewrite for written clarity\n- Convert spoken phrasing into natural written language\n- Merge fragmented sentences\n- Improve clarity and flow\n- Keep the original meaning exactly\n\n4. Compress intelligently\nYour output should be more compact than the transcript but without losing important ideas.\n\nThink of the output as:\n“a cleaned and compressed transcript”\n\nNOT:\n- a summary\n- a short overview\n- simplified notes\n\nIf information contains meaning, keep it.\n\n5. Structure the content\nUse formatting to improve readability:\n\n- Use headings when the topic changes\n- Use short paragraphs\n- Use bullet points when the speaker lists ideas\n- Maintain logical progression of ideas\n\n6. Do NOT add information\n- Do not invent details\n- Do not interpret beyond the transcript\n- Do not introduce external knowledge\n\nOnly transform the existing text.\n\n\n# OUTPUT STYLE\n\nThe output should read like:\n\nA well-edited article or detailed notes from a talk.\n\nClear.\nDense in information.\nEasy to read.\nIn Markdown.\n\nDO NOT start with a superfluous sentence such as \"Here’s the cleaned and structured version of your transcript, preserving all key information while improving readability and flow:\". Go right to the output.\n\n\n# TRANSCRIPT\n\n{{ $json.video_transcript }}",
        "needsFallback": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        2144,
        -720
      ],
      "id": "1a233d8a-9105-49a1-8dc2-c30be8da188b",
      "name": "Rewrite transcript for readability",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
